1
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,473
Hi, Grandpa.

2
00:00:26,473 --> 00:00:27,800
Hi, Robbie.

3
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:29,215
Can I help?

4
00:00:29,215 --> 00:00:31,200
Yes, indeed.

5
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:34,200
Hand me two eggs from the refrigerator,

6
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:38,200
and I'll make you two fried eggs.

7
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:40,200
How about some bacon?

8
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:43,100
I made enough for an army.

9
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:45,200
You going to the baseball game today?

10
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:49,300
It's a perfect day for it--a little cloudy but nice and warm.

11
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:50,917
Dad and I were planning to go to the game,

12
00:00:50,917 --> 00:00:52,000
but he has to work today,

13
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,200
and my friends don't want to go.

14
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:56,239
It's not an important game, anyway.

15
00:00:56,239 --> 00:00:58,900
Do you have any other plans for the day?

16
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:00,400
I'll work on my computer.

17
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:03,388
I have a new math program, and I want to learn how to use it.

18
00:01:03,388 --> 00:01:04,737
Maybe you can teach me

19
00:01:04,737 --> 00:01:06,500
how to work on a computer someday.

20
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:09,714
Anytime. It's really easy, but, like anything,

21
00:01:09,714 --> 00:01:13,660
you need to work at it, Grandpa.

22
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:14,600
This bacon is great.

23
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:17,479
I love crispy bacon.

24
00:01:17,479 --> 00:01:19,200
Oh, what are you doing tomorrow?

25
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:22,200
Nothing much.

26
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:26,710
Well, maybe your dad and I could take you fishing with us.

27
00:01:26,710 --> 00:01:28,267
I'd like that, but ...

28
00:01:28,267 --> 00:01:30,800
But what?

29
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:32,484
But Dad is always so busy.

30
00:01:32,484 --> 00:01:37,800
Well, can you come fishing with me tomorrow?

31
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:41,200
Sure, I can.

32
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:44,200
Robbie says you can't take him to the game today.

33
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,200
I really feel bad about it,

34
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:46,600
but they need me at the hospital today,

35
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:48,500
in the children's ward.

36
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:50,900
I understand.

37
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:52,800
Maybe we can spend some time together next weekend.

38
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:53,760
Definitely.

39
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:54,500
We should.

40
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:57,688
You and Robbie and me.

41
00:01:57,688 --> 00:01:59,800
Remember our first fishing trip?

42
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:01,200
I sure do....

43
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:04,900
Well, I've got to run, Dad.

44
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:08,200
See you later.

45
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:09,400
Going fishing?

46
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:12,200
I'm thinking about it....

47
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,924
So, how's work?

48
00:02:13,924 --> 00:02:16,756
Oh, the usual problems.

49
00:02:16,756 --> 00:02:18,400
You're working pretty hard these days.

50
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:22,900
I guess I am.

51
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:26,259
When did you last go fishing with Robbie?

52
00:02:26,259 --> 00:02:28,000
I remember exactly.

53
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,800
It was on his birthday, June second, two years ago.

54
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:36,087
We didn't catch anything.

55
00:02:36,087 --> 00:02:38,200
Remember our fishing trips?

56
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:43,100
Yes. I loved them.

57
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:46,305
Remember catching your first fish?

58
00:02:46,305 --> 00:02:47,100
How can I forget?

59
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:51,445
I fell out of the boat!

60
00:02:51,445 --> 00:02:53,100
We had some good times together.

61
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:56,106
Yes, we did.

62
00:02:56,106 --> 00:02:59,100
Maybe we should do it again.

63
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:00,900
How about tomorrow?

64
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:02,600
Don't you have to work?

65
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:05,111
My paper work will wait.

66
00:03:05,111 --> 00:03:07,800
Oh, Robbie will be thrilled.

67
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:09,800
I am, too, Son.

68
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,165
I want to spend more time with Robbie.

69
00:03:11,165 --> 00:03:12,600
Tomorrow.

70
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:14,800
It'll be like old times for you and me.

71
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:17,971
And Robbie will love it.

72
00:03:17,971 --> 00:03:21,200
Well, what's the weather going to be like?

73
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:27,800
Radio says sunny and mild.

74
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:31,428
Well, I'll tell Robbie.

75
00:03:31,428 --> 00:03:35,000
And thanks, Dad.

76
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,200
Don't thank me.

77
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:39,200
I'm just being a grandfather.
